From 252e7dbf0038ca7bcd815aa298d36747218c6cda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: utzcoz <utzcoz@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 11:37:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] util/rust: implement the sys layer for macOS

mesa3d_util supported Linux and Windows; macOS resolved to the stub backend,
whose entry points are unimplemented. Implement it, so that the guest driver
and the kumquat transport built on top of it work on macOS.

The primitives macOS lacks are emulated with the closest equivalent:

- No AF_UNIX SOCK_SEQPACKET, so packet tubes are framed over SOCK_STREAM
  with an 8-byte [payload length][descriptor count] header. The descriptors
  ride on the header via SCM_RIGHTS, and a message is reassembled with as
  many recvmsg calls as it takes. receive() checks the descriptor count it
  was promised against the one it got.
- No MSG_NOSIGNAL, so tube sockets carry SO_NOSIGPIPE: writing to a closed
  peer yields EPIPE rather than killing a host process that has not reset
  SIGPIPE.
- Accepted sockets inherit the listener's file status flags on BSD-derived
  systems, unlike Linux. The listener is non-blocking so that accepting
  never stalls an event loop, so accept() clears O_NONBLOCK again: the calls
  that reassemble the rest of a message must wait for it rather than fail
  with EAGAIN.
- No eventfd. An event has to be a single descriptor that can be both
  signalled and waited on, and that keeps working once duplicated into
  another process, because either side may be the one to signal. A
  self-connected AF_UNIX SOCK_DGRAM socket has that property. It has to be
  bound to a path first, which is done inside a per-event mode 0700
  directory so that no other local process can win a race to the name; both
  the socket and the directory are removed as soon as it is connected.
- No memfd_create, so anonymous shared memory is shm_open followed
  immediately by shm_unlink.
- No epoll, so the wait context is built on kqueue.
- No /proc/self/fd, so descriptors are classified from their stat file type
  and open flags rather than from a symlink target.
- No futex. os_sync_wait_on_address and os_sync_wake_by_address_* are the
  platform equivalent. They have no bitset, which only filters which waiters
  a wake reaches, so a wake reaches a superset of them; waiters re-check the
  value they waited on, so that is harmless.

Everything goes through rustix, which mesa3d_util already depends on, so
this adds no new crate dependency and needs no build changes.
